  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Which iOS devices are running Ion, on what version, paired to which server?\n\nThe per-device mobile view over the **iOS log stream** (`{service_name=\"ion-ios\", event_name=\"\"}`). iOS emits no telemetry, so this pack does not appear on [Ion Fleet](/d/ion-fleet) — it reads the operational logs the paired server collects.\n\nEvery line carries **device identity** stamped by iOS: `device_id` (stable per-device UUID from `identifierForVendor` — survives re-pairings), `device_model` (hardware model e.g. `iPhone15,3`), OS version, and app version+build. On MDM-enrolled devices, `mdm_device_id` and `mdm_serial` enable cross-reference to Intune. The server stamps `pairing_id` (the ECDH channel ID for the specific pairing session) and `desktop_host`.\n\nThe **device→server pairing** table below is the \"which device connected where\" matrix. `desktop_host` matches the telemetry `host`, so a pairing row cross-references the Fleet board for the same machine.\n\nAll panels honor the dashboard time picker except **Device last-seen**, a liveness detector with a fixed 24h lookback so a quiet device stays visible.\n\n| Related | Dashboard |\n|---|---|\n| Landing | [Ion Overview](/d/ion-overview) |\n| Server/host view | [Ion Fleet](/d/ion-fleet) |\n| Live logs | [Ion Live Logs](/d/ion-logs) |"
      },
      "datasource": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Devices reporting",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "blue"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": []
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "noValue": "no iOS logs"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "count(sum by (device_id) (count_over_time({service_name=\"ion-ios\", event_name=\"\", host_name=~\"$host\", user=~\"$user\"} | json device_id=\"fields.device_id\", device_model=\"fields.device_model\", pairing_id=\"fields.pairing_id\", desktop_host=\"fields.desktop_host\", app_version=\"fields.app_version\", app_build=\"fields.app_build\", os_version=\"fields.os_version\", mdm_device_id=\"fields.mdm_device_id\", mdm_serial=\"fields.mdm_serial\" | __error__=\"\" | device_model=~\"$device\" [$__range])))",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "refId": "A",
          "__ionClass": "accumulation"
        }
      ]
    },
